  "source": "Roland D-50 factory patch I-11, PN-D50-00, with the changes below",
  "changes": [
    "Upper partial 2, the soft octave below the key, fades from >A#1 (tva_bias_point 65) rather than >A#2 (77): played here, it was as loud as partial 1 up to C3, which sounded too low there, while recordings of a D-50 have its octave below the key subtle from C3 up and strong at C2 only, as Eric Persing, who made the patch, describes it: a very soft, subtle lower octave."
